00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:41.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, perfect. All right, well, do you guys have any questions before I share my screen and we dive in?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Mm-mm.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, sounds good.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, can you all see my screen?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. So, we had it noted from your onboarding questionnaire that total ads budget is $2,000 a month. And what we would suggest is splitting that evenly between Google and Meta.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Yes.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:30.000
Whitney Hodges: start. Now, as data, you know, begins coming in, and if we're kind of starting to see that one platform is performing more strongly than another, then we can kind of change up allocations at that point. But to start, we just recommend doing an even split.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:36.000
Whitney Hodges: So, Carmen, do you want to speak to the Google Ads side of things in a bit more detail?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes. So with the type of campaign that I chose, so there's multiple different types of campaigns.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Alina: Nope, you're muted.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Oh, I'm sorry. I meant to mute myself.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Oh.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Sorry.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.000
Alina: You're still muted, sweetie.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mute. Can you hear me now?

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Alina: Yeah.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, perfect. Okay, so there's different types of campaigns on Google, and so the main one I chose is the search campaign. So with search campaigns, these aren't pop-ups on random different sites with pictures, it's just people search for a wedding venue in that Atlanta area, and then they see your website pop up at the top. So it's SEO, basically, with a credit card.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, and so then when I create this campaign, I'll have it with the objective of being leads, but I'm gonna tell Google to get as many clicks onto the site right now versus leads because, uh, I want to get data in. So Google doesn't really know.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:50.000
Carmen Cruickshank: how to maximize leads, unless they know who the types of people that become a lead are. So normally, in the first month, I'll just try to get all those clicks there for cheap, because we pay based on clicks, not on how many people see it. So on Meta, you know, you pay per thousand people that see it.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:08:07.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Google, you pay based on the person clicking. Uh, and then after about a month or 6 weeks, once Google can tell who's a lead, then I switch it to maximize leads. That way, we actually really double down on that. Do you guys have any questions so far on the strategy there, or anything?

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Okay.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, I'm glad. And then for the landing page right now, I'll have it be the weddings page, of course, because that speaks to people directly searching for you guys and clicking on the ad.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And again, it'll be $33.33 a day. As for location, I know you guys mentioned a lot of different areas in there. I know it'll be generally the metro area of Atlanta, uh, but I assume you guys wanted it expanded more, is that correct?

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.000
Alina: Yeah, thank you.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:48.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, yeah, I just put in there all the different locations you put. Sometimes those specific locations are in Google Ads, sometimes not, but I'll go over it with you guys and show you a visual before I launch it, just to make sure it's all approved.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:09:05.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Um, and as for targeting, I know, of course, it's mainly women doing the planning, but I'm just leaving it open to women and men. Uh, and I know your guys' ideal client is in their mid-20s to late-30s, but again, I'm just kind of leaving ages open. If I see a super young crowd or a super, like.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:21.000
Carmen Cruickshank: 65 plus is just not converting, maybe they're clicking but not becoming a lead, then I can exclude them in the future, but for now, again, we'll just keep it open. And then I can also target different people based on their interests, so that's called audience segments in Google Ads, so people searching for.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:39.000
Carmen Cruickshank: wedding rings or dresses, they're in wedding planning, soon to be married, Google can just kind of tell. So, just again, to get that extra targeting. Uh, and then I am glad you guys do have an actual thank you page to track leads, so anytime Google sees that someone comes onto the thank you page from clicking on an ad, that's when it's an official.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:46.000
Carmen Cruickshank: lead form submission. Uh, so that's all really on the overall strategy. Do you guys, again, have any questions on that?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): No.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.000
Alina: Pretty straightforward.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:58.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, that's pretty straightforward. Okay, so now we're gonna look at keywords. So this is how I tell Google who to show the ad to, so people searching these keywords in general.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So, normally we need 5 to 10, so again, these are not…

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:17.000
Carmen Cruickshank: a whole list. But I put wedding venue, wedding venue in Georgia, wedding halls in Georgia, wedding reception venues, Atlanta, Georgia, outdoor wedding venues, Atlanta, Georgia, wedding venue near Atlanta, intimate wedding venues, estate.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:29.000
Carmen Cruickshank: equestrian, or kind of like a mansion vibe in some way. I didn't really want to put mansion, because I know that you guys are not really marketed that way. Equestrian didn't have a lot of search volume. You can see…

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:34.000
Alina: Well, we don't… we don't have a mansion on this property. We do have a mansion, but it's on a totally separate property, and we're not.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:48.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Exactly. That's why I didn't really want to put anything like that in here. I wanted to keep it relevant with enough search volume, so I like to look for anything 40 or above. I can tell what people… how many people are searching per month in that Atlanta area for that keyword.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:54.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So, that's just a good idea there. But is there any other keywords you guys wanted to add here, or at least try?

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I mean, I just want to hit the highest ones. I mean, if you've looked, I mean, I know, like, Wedding Venue Near Me and stuff like that, Wedding Venue Generic, it's got the biggest one, so I think that kind of… what you have there kind of hits it.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.000
Alina: Okay.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I think it's fine.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Good to know. Anything on your mind?

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): There is…

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Oh, uh-huh.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): No, that's fine. Go ahead, Alina. Anything?

