Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:16.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): No.

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Sounds good. Any other questions or concerns that we can help with at this point?

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:33.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): So, one of the things that I'm always really curious about is just, like, how these ads are working. Is that part of the flow for you guys with…

00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:46.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): will we have, like, a monthly report of some kind to be, like, these ads worked well, these didn't? How will we, like, not micromanage, but just out of curiosity, will we be able to see some data?

00:28:46.000 --> 00:29:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes, yeah, so there's a monthly report that will be emailed over to you every month that includes the analytics and, you know, kind of what we are seeing on our end. And then, of course, we'll also, you know, start scheduling the monthly.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:51.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Okay.

00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:53.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Awesome.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Strategy call, um, where if you have any questions about ad performance, we can speak to that on the call as well.

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:22.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): That's great. So, just correct me if I'm wrong, with the allocation of the $1,000, with the Google ad, it's kind of like an amount of money that you stick in there, and it may not always be used, right?

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:35.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): So, I mean, you may say you could spend up to $1,000, but if people aren't clicking on it, you're not actually spending $1,000. But for Meta, it's gonna… it'll take every penny, right? So if you tell it to put it out.

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.000
Whitney Hodges: So I mean, it'll be.

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:38.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): $1,000, it'll spend $1,000.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:40.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Am I wrong?

00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:40.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I know.

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, I can speak at least for the Google side. Normally, the businesses that have $1,000 but don't normally spend all that are very niche, and people don't search for them, so I think you guys would get your full $1,000 spent on Google.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:30:01.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Okay, especially for using some of the big target words that have 9,000 clicks.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, exactly.

00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Yeah, makes sense.

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:04.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, and on the Meta Ads side, yes, you're right. You know, over there, it is pay per impression, so it's all about paying for visibility versus paying for clicks on the Google Ads side, so whatever the daily budget is set at.

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:35.000
Whitney Hodges: You know, it is going to spend that. Yeah, but the budget is going to be split between, you know, campaigns that are going to completely cold audiences, the campaigns that are meant for lead generation, and the retargeting.

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:23.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): They'll use it, yeah.

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:39.000
Whitney Hodges: campaigns that are strictly going to your warm audience.

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:54.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): I guess I just… I… I'm… we're fine doing this, because Alina wants to just, like, shotgun it, and I'm totally fine with that, but I'm in even a more competitive market, and I never spend $1,000 a month on my Google ad. I think I… the max I ever spent was, like, $750.

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:30:54.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): So, I guess I just want to know, like, you know, if there'd be further conversation to be like, you know, you might not need to be spending as much as that, you know, on your Google ad. We could tighten that up a little.

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:09.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): Not saying that I want to do that now, but I just want to know, like.

00:31:10.000 --> 00:31:12.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): If there will be a way to track.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:17.000
Tirzah's iPhone (2): that it would be fine to lower our spend, you know, once we get some more traction.

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, I think that's definitely feasible, like, we could definitely check if there's any areas of opportunity to, like, take down the budget, like you said, from $1,000 to $750 if we see things are spent inefficiently. Uh, but yeah, we can definitely do that.

00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:35.000
